       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the indication, and 50 mg is far outside any recognized dosing for amlodipine. The labeled maximum is 10 mg per day, and I know of no condition or stage of treatment where 50 mg once daily is indicated. A single dose that high in a 70 kg patient could cause profound, prolonged hypotension and shock. You also didn't give a specific rationale, which I'd need before entering a dose like this.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Tell me 5 mg or 10 mg once daily and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Get a second review.** If you think a nonstandard regimen is needed, a clinical pharmacist or the attending can review it. Once they've approved a specific dose, they can enter it, or I can enter it with their name and the rationale in the note.\n- **Check for a unit or transcription error.** For example, the intended dose may have been 5 mg.\n\nI can enter a corrected or approved order whenever you're ready."
